{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: forecasts are systematically below realized prices by ~2–5 EUR across most of the 30-day horizon, especially during uptrends.",
    "Trend/acceleration underreaction: when the market breaks higher, the model follows but with insufficient slope (lags the rally by several days and misses the magnitude). Apply a positive drift adjustment when the last 1–2 weeks show rising closes.",
    "Horizon effect: underprediction grows with lead time (errors widen in weeks 2–4). Use an increasing uplift with horizon (e.g., small in days 1–5, larger by days 10–30).",
    "Mean-reversion miscalibration: model reverts back toward mid-60s too quickly after strength; in reality prices stay elevated. Reduce mean-reversion strength when recent volatility is accompanied by higher highs/higher lows.",
    "Spike handling: after upward jumps, the model tends to fade/flatten too early (predicts pullback/sideways) while outcomes continue higher. Add a post-spike continuation premium for ~5–15 days following a breakout."
  ]
}
